  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1a8da173e69a9bd42921b4e60f3377d5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Turn Structure
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CardCreator.CardDefinition
  referenceText: '<b>SETUP</b> 20 life. Draw 5. Each deck: 20 creatures + 1 evolution
    kept aside. Board: 5 columns, front and rear.


    <color=#EBCB82><b>1  READY</b></color>
    Ready your creatures. Reset once-per-turn effects. A Webbed arrival skips its
    next ready step.


    <color=#EBCB82><b>2  DRAW</b></color> Draw 1. First player
    skips their first draw. If you must draw from an empty deck, you lose.


    <color=#EBCB82><b>3 
    REAR</b></color> You may place 1 creature from hand in an empty rear zone for
    free, exhausted.


    <color=#EBCB82><b>4  ACT</b></color> Take up to 2 actions:
    play a front creature, move one front creature sideways 1 zone, or change stance.
    Exhaust ready rear creatures to pay printed Essence costs. New creatures enter
    exhausted.


    <color=#EBCB82><b>5  BATTLE</b></color> Each ready front creature
    in Attack stance may attack once down its column; exhaust it. Guard may intercept.
    Deal simultaneous damage; an open lane hits life. Resolve abilities and Triumph
    after each battle.


    <color=#EBCB82><b>6  END</b></color> End temporary bonuses.
    Damage and Scars remain. Pass the turn. At 0 life, you lose.'
